<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Banu Kilab</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Kilab</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Banu Kilab were an Arab tribe of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qays">Qays</a> group who migrated from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arabia">Arabia</a> to northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/syria">Syria</a> in the 10th century. They raided and pressed the rulers of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aleppo">Aleppo</a>, and in 1024 their chief <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/salih-ibn-mirdas">Salih ibn Mirdas</a> took the city and founded the Mirdasid <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emirate">emirate</a>. The tribe remained powerful in the region until the Seljuk period.</p></div>
